# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The team portal must never be served from a stale browser cache. Pages
# defaults static assets to `max-age=14400` (4 hours), which once left every
# logged-in browser running a broken auth.js for hours after the fix had
# already shipped — and because the bug was a redirect loop, the page never
# settled long enough for the browser to revalidate on its own.
#
# `no-cache` does NOT mean "don't store": the browser still keeps the file and
# still gets a cheap 304 when nothing changed. It only means "always ask
# first", so a fix reaches people on their next load instead of hours later.
/team/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
